1. WRONG ENDPOINT. `/v1/agent/turn` is served on the board at `http://127.0.0.1:8766` (loopback agent listener; `ss` shows middleware-service on 127.0.0.1:8766). Send every request FROM THE BOARD via `adb shell curl ... http://127.0.0.1:8766/v1/agent/turn`, exactly like round 46 did — copy the request shape/headers from `scratch/r46-20261008/B1.txt`, `B2.txt` (x-session-id header, JSON body file under /data/local/tmp). Do not use host port forwards for the agent endpoint. A 404 from 8765 is your routing mistake, not a test result.
2. FALSE "start-post timeout". The lines `6月 26 19:27:09 ... start-post operation timed out` in your evidence are months-old journal history (identical to round 43's), not this run. You again selected logs by date. Use `logger -t handoff48 <marker>` before each step and read only journal lines after that marker (`journalctl -u middleware-service --no-pager | sed -n '/handoff48 <marker>/,$p'` or `--cursor`), and verify the PID matches the process you started.
3. LEFTOVER PROCESS. You reported temporary proxy files removed, but `python3 /data/local/tmp/handoff48/proxy.py` (pid 13085) was still listening on 127.0.0.1:18080 after your run. The coordinator killed it and removed /data/local/tmp/handoff48. In cleanup, verify with `ss -ltnp | grep 18080` (must be empty) and `ps -ef | grep proxy.py` before claiming removal.
4. The proxy approach from round 46 worked (`scratch/r46-20261008/proxy-start.log`): start the proxy, point `cloud_base_url` at it, restart middleware-service ONCE, then run all cases.

The binary you built (sha 59ecbec3…) is still in `target/aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu/release/` — reuse it if its sha matches; otherwise rebuild in the foreground. Run cases 1–5 per the spec, amend the REPORT Update 48 (replace the invalid run with a short note that it was an operator error), commit, and end with the spec's final message. Do not end your turn before that.
